    Q10: GUARD -- that factor 2 relates two definitions of the SAME vacuum energy, both functions of Z~ alone; it contains no a0 and no beta, and adopting it as kappa's 1/2 would be exactly the convention-choosing the branch rule forbids.  Recorded so it is never adopted.
  [FAIL] Q10 [alternative, Brown-York] the quasi-local energy at the de Sitter horizon relates Z to beta   (E_BY = c^4 L_dS/G is purely geometric (L_dS is fixed by eps = Z~q^2/2 alone) and is invariant under the Q5 map; the factor 2 between E_BY and the volume integral is a property of the horizon, not of a0)

  OUTCOME: flux quantisation CANNOT fix Z/beta^2, and the obstruction is as sharp as k01's zero mode -- it is its multiplicative twin.
           WHAT QUANTISATION DOES (Q4): the membrane makes the conjugate momentum P_q jump by e, so q_n = n e/Z~ and eps_n = n^2 e^2/(2 Z~);
           adding the Brown-Teitelboim terminal condition Delta eps = 6 pi G T^2 fixes the flux sector COMPLETELY, Z~ = (2n-1)e^2/(12 pi G T^2).
           WHAT IT CANNOT DO (Q5, the theorem): every membrane- and geometry-sector quantity -- the quantisation condition, the spectrum, the
           step, the junction radius, Lambda, L_dS, the boundary term, E_BY -- is a function of the SUM Z~ = Z + 2 b beta^2 and of (e, T, G, n).
           kappa^2 = 2 beta^2/Z~ needs the SPLIT of Z~ between the four-form's own stiffness Z and the MOND-promoted piece 2 b beta^2.
           The map beta -> mu beta, Z -> Z + 2 b beta^2 (1 - mu^2) holds the entire quantised sector fixed and sends kappa -> mu kappa.
           MECHANISM: charge quantisation constrains couplings to the POTENTIAL A_3 (a topological pairing, hence integer-valued); beta
           multiplies the gauge-invariant FIELD STRENGTH q inside a nonlinear function, so it carries no charge, and a 2-brane in D = 4 has no
           magnetic partner (a -2 brane) to pair with in a Dirac condition.  Positivity of Z bounds kappa only by 1/sqrt(b) = 7.45.
           COST IMPORTED (Q7): quantisation forces the membrane charge to sit AT the scale it should explain, sqrt(e) <= 2.7 meV; a Planckian
           charge overshoots rho_Lambda by 4e+122 at n = 1 -- BP's problem, which they solve with many flux directions (Q2: J >= 81, i.e.
           an exponentially large landscape of levels), not with a coefficient.
           GUARD (Q8): the '8' is not an integer target.  2/kappa^2 - 2b is 7.96 on the canonical footing but 5.48 on the alt footing (31%).
           BOUNDARY SECTOR (Q9, Q10): the GHY term carries no matter coupling; the four-form boundary term re-derives k04's F1 sign and sees Z~ only;
           Brown-York at the horizon gives E = c^4 L_dS/G, exactly 2x the volume integral -- a factor 2 that is NOT kappa and is logged as a guard.
           STILL UNTESTED (the one adjacent door): a membrane that itself carries MOND charge, so that T or e depend on a0.  That is a different
           model with a new coupling, not this one; it is not closed here and is not claimed to be.

RESULT: 5 FAIL -> ['Q6 [requirement] quantisation plus the membrane tension express Z/beta^2 in terms of (e, T, G, integers)', 'Q7 [requirement] the observed rho_Lambda is reached with an integer n >= 1 for a membrane charge at an independently motivated scale (both footings)', 'Q8 [numerology guard] the target ratio is a footing- and kernel-robust integer that an integer-valued principle could plausibly hit', "Q9 [alternative, boundary term] the Gibbons-Hawking-York term or the four-form's own boundary term relates Z to beta", 'Q10 [alternative, Brown-York] the quasi-local energy at the de Sitter horizon relates Z to beta']
